.TH VALIDATE-AUTONOMOUS-PHASE-RESULT 1 "September 2026" "autonomous-run-governance 0.4.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
validate-autonomous-phase-result \- validate semantic completion of one routed phase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validate-autonomous-phase-result.sh
.BR --repo " PATH"
.BR --result " FILE"
.BR --phase-id " ID"
.RB [ --attempt-id " UUID"]
.BR --exit-code " N"
.BR --expected-tasks " N"
.BR --expected-payload " PATH"
.BR --gate-exit-code " N"
.RB [ --task-manifest " PATH"]
.RB [ --task-inventory-sha " SHA256"]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A process exit code of zero is necessary but not sufficient. The command also
checks the structured result schema, phase and attempt identity, task
completion, gate result, payload path, and normalized payload SHA-256.
The accepted task count and payload path must be fixed before the model runs;
the gate exit code must come from an independent postflight check.
.PP
DE: Fehlende, leere, abgeschnittene, blockierte oder fachlich unvollstaendige
Ergebnisse bleiben fehlgeschlossen und duerfen nicht als Completed gespeichert
werden.
.PP
EN: Missing, empty, truncated, blocked, or semantically incomplete results fail
closed and must not be persisted as Completed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --repo PATH
Repository root used to resolve the repository-relative payload path.
.TP
.B --result FILE
Structured JSON result emitted by the routed phase.
.TP
.B --phase-id ID
Expected stable phase identifier.
.TP
.B --attempt-id UUID
Expected attempt identifier. The routing runner supplies it to reject results
from earlier attempts; standalone historical inspection may omit it.
.TP
.B --exit-code N
Exit code of the completed phase process.
.TP
.B --expected-tasks N
Positive task count accepted before runner execution.
.TP
.B --expected-payload PATH
Repository-relative path of the accepted phase artifact.
.TP
.B --gate-exit-code N
Exit code of an independent phase gate check.
.TP
.B --task-manifest PATH
Optional accepted implementation checklist; its item count and completion are verified.
.TP
.B --task-inventory-sha SHA256
Hash of the task identities captured before runner execution; required with a task manifest.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means semantic completion passed. Two means invocation or malformed input
failed. Three means process or semantic phase completion failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
invoke-autonomous-model-phase(1), validate-autonomous-delivery-set(1)
